    "type": "p",
    "md": "Two shapes of question. A matching exercise, often the last on the paper, gives one mark per line and no method marks, so recognition is the whole job. A draw-it question gives marks for the plotted points and for a curve that is genuinely curved. Stuck: name the family from the highest power, then sketch the shape you know it has."
